Hands-on Lab 1: Install Git
Windows

Download Git from the official website:

Git for Windows

Verify:

git --version
Hands-on Lab 2: Configure Git
git config --global user.name "Anusha"
git config --global user.email "your-email@example.com"

Check configuration:

git config --list
Hands-on Lab 3: Create Your First Repository
mkdir git-demo
cd git-demo

Initialize Git:

git init

Expected output:

Initialized empty Git repository
Hands-on Lab 4: Create First File
echo "Hello Azure DevOps" > README.md

Check status:

git status

You'll see:

Untracked files:
README.md
Hands-on Lab 5: Stage the File
git add README.md

Check status again:

git status

Now it should appear under Changes to be committed.

Hands-on Lab 6: Commit
git commit -m "Initial Commit"

View history:

git log

You'll see your first commit with its SHA hash.

Hands-on Lab 7: Create a GitHub Repository
Create a new repository in GitHub.
Do not initialize it with a README.
Connect your local repository:
git remote add origin <repository-url>

Verify:

git remote -v

Push:

git branch -M main
git push -u origin main
