Key Takeaways
Git is a Distributed Version Control System.
The Git workflow is:
Working Directory → Staging Area → Local Repository → Remote Repository.
Every commit is identified by a unique SHA hash.
Commits remain local until you push them.
Git is the starting point for every modern CI/CD pipeline.
